Subject: [PATCH] agent: refuse an init-data-supplied agent policy

The agent policy is the measured /etc/kata-opa/default-policy.rego on the
dm-verity root, and its CreateContainerRequest rules are what bind a
container's enforced digest to the bytes the guest pulls. set_policy()
replaces the engine outright, and the init-data document is written by the
host: its sha256 lands in HOST_DATA, but nothing in the guest compares that
against what the c8s webhook stamped, so the host can hand the guest its own
policy.rego and drop every rule. `SetPolicyRequest := false` does not cover
this path -- it never reaches allow_request.

c8s never puts policy.rego in the document it builds (c8s/pkg/initdata), so
refusing outright is exact: any document carrying one was not ours.

--- a/src/agent/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/agent/src/main.rs
@@ -415,17 +415,15 @@
         init_attestation_components(logger, config, &initdata_return_value).await?;
     }
 
-    // if policy is given via initdata, use it
+    // c8s: the policy is the measured baked file. init-data is host-written
+    // and unverified in the guest, so a policy delivered there would replace
+    // it; fail the boot rather than enforce the host's rules.
     #[cfg(feature = "agent-policy")]
     if let Some(initdata_return_value) = initdata_return_value {
-        if let Some(policy) = &initdata_return_value._policy {
-            info!(logger, "using policy from initdata");
-            AGENT_POLICY
-                .lock()
-                .await
-                .set_policy(policy)
-                .await
-                .context("Failed to set policy from initdata")?;
+        if initdata_return_value._policy.is_some() {
+            return Err(anyhow!(
+                "init-data carries an agent policy; this guest enforces the measured baked policy only"
+            ));
         }
     }
 
